{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLGVBL2SCTh5SiFiTST8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed this, but only through `exptrigsimp`. Plain `trigsimp(f)` still returns the exponential form unchanged.\n\nWhat works now:\n- `exptrigsimp(f)` returns `sin(k)`.\n- `exptrigsimp(f/k)` returns `sin(k)/k`.\n- `exptrigsimp(f/k).rewrite(sinc)` returns `sinc(k)`.\n\nThe two changes:\n1. **`sympy/simplify/trigsimp.py`**: before this fix, `exptrigsimp` rewrote the sum in terms of `cos` and `sin` but never multiplied the brackets back out. So the pieces that cancel down to `sin(k)` stayed hidden, and the original form looked simpler. For a sum, it now also tries the multiplied-out version and keeps whichever form is smallest.\n2. **`sympy/functions/elementary/trigonometric.py`**: added a rewrite rule so `sin(x).rewrite(sinc)` gives `x*sinc(x)`. Simplification doesn't produce `sinc` on its own; you have to ask for the rewrite.\n\nI ran the tests in `test_trigsimp.py`, `test_simplify.py` and `test_trigonometric.py`: 122 pass and 4 fail. The same 4 fail without my changes: `test_issue_6811_fail`, `test_factorial_simplify`, `test_simplify_float_vs_integer` and `test_sin_cos_with_infinity`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":503,"cache_read_input_tokens":24297,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":503},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07bc00a4-52c5-4c53-b127-a8d0643ce6fc","uuid":"e01b4253-af17-42de-8815-9d8711977ecf","timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:38:48.661Z","request_id":"req_011ChLGVBA6fSgFMCQ9Tpz5u"}
